      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From a theoretical standpoint, designing a compound to selectively target dopamine or hunger receptors and disperse it invisibly via HVAC is extremely complex and would require cutting-edge, highly controlled technology. If such a substance were used, sophisticated chemical analysis and air quality monitoring would be necessary to detect it, as even trace amounts of novel compounds can be identified. Concealing it as a mundane \"ambient scent\" might fool a casual observer, but environmental scientists could potentially test air samples for unusual chemical signatures.",
